data: {"sections":[{"section_id":"header","type":"template","content":"LEGAL NOTICE\n(Under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908)\n\nDate: 06 May 2026\n\nTo,\nThe Executive Engineer, Road Construction Department, Government of Jharkhand\nProject Bhawan, Doranda, Ranchi - 834002\n\nFrom,\nM/s Chotanagpur Construction Co.\nThrough: Adv. Pradeep Topno, Advocate\nChamber No. 18, Jharkhand High Court Bar Association, Ranchi - 834001","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"subject_line","type":"template","content":"Subject: Legal Notice under Section 80 CPC — prior to institution of suit against the Government / Public Officer\n\nSir/Madam,\n\nUnder instructions from and on behalf of my client, M/s Chotanagpur Construction Co., I hereby serve upon you this legal notice under Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908, and call upon you to note the following:","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"body","type":"ai_generated","content":"1. My client M/s Chotanagpur Construction Co. is a reputed construction company engaged in the business of civil construction works including road construction, building construction and infrastructure development projects across Jharkhand State. My client has been successfully executing various government contracts with impeccable track record and has maintained highest standards of workmanship and timely completion of projects entrusted to them.\n\n2. My client was awarded the contract for road widening and resurfacing of Ranchi-Khunti Road (SH-4) vide Work Order No. JRCD/RAN/2025/042 dated 20.08.2025 for a contract value of Rs. 1,85,00,000/- (Rupees One Crore Eighty Five Lakh only). The said work order was issued by your office and my client accepted the same and commenced the contracted work with due diligence and in accordance with the specifications and timelines mentioned therein.\n\n3. My client diligently executed the entire contracted work as per the approved plans, specifications and quality parameters and completed all contracted work by 15.01.2026, well within the stipulated time frame. Upon completion, my client submitted the final running bills along with measurement books which were duly verified and certified by the site engineer appointed by your department, confirming the satisfactory completion of the work as per contract specifications.\n\n4. Despite the satisfactory completion of work and submission of all requisite documents, my client has made repeated representations to your office seeking release of the outstanding final payment. The representations were made vide letters dated 10.02.2026, 15.03.2026, and 25.04.2026, copies of which are available on record. However, no positive response has been received from your end nor has any clarification been sought regarding the delay in payment.\n\n5. The final payment of Rs. 62,30,000/- (Rupees Sixty Two Lakh Thirty Thousand only) remains outstanding since 15.01.2026, which constitutes a substantial amount due and payable to my client as per the terms and conditions of the work order. The wrongful withholding of the said amount has caused severe financial hardship to my client who has outstanding vendor liabilities and is facing difficulties in meeting their business obligations due to non-payment of legitimate dues.\n\n6. It is pertinent to mention that Section 80 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908 mandates that no suit shall be instituted against the Government or any public officer in respect of any act purporting to be done by such public officer in his official capacity, until the expiration of two months next after notice in writing has been delivered to or left at the office of such Government or public officer.\n\n7. In compliance with the aforesaid mandatory provision, this legal notice is being served upon you to provide an opportunity to settle the matter amicably before resorting to legal proceedings. The withholding of legitimate dues without any justifiable reason constitutes breach of contractual obligations and amounts to causing wrongful loss to my client.\n\n8. NOTICE is hereby served upon you to release the outstanding final payment of Rs. 62,30,000/- along with applicable interest as per contract terms within a period of sixty (60) days from the receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings for recovery of the said amount along with interest, damages and costs, without any further reference to you."},{"section_id":"demand_clause","type":"template","content":"DEMAND\n\nYou are hereby called upon to release the outstanding payment of Rs. 62,30,000/- along with interest at the rate of 12% per annum from 15.01.2026 till actual payment, and pay damages of Rs. 3,00,000/- for the wrongful withholding within a period of two (2) months from the date of receipt of this notice, failing which my client shall be constrained to initiate appropriate legal proceedings before the competent civil court, at your risk, cost, and consequences, without any further reference to you.","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"closing","type":"template","content":"A copy of this notice is retained in my office for record and further action.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n\n_________________________\nAdv. Pradeep Topno\nAdvocate\nEnrollment No. JHC/2845/2017\nChamber No. 18, Jharkhand High Court Bar Association, Ranchi - 834001\n\n(Counsel for M/s Chotanagpur Construction Co.)","alignment":"left"},{"section_id":"disclaimer","type":"template","content":"AI-assisted draft — verify with applicable law before filing. Lawie does not provide legal advice.","alignment":"center","style":"footer_small_gray"}]}

event: checklist
data: {"items":["Send via Registered Post AD (Acknowledgement Due) — retain receipt","Send additional copy via Speed Post","Retain photocopy of notice with postal receipts","Keep proof of delivery (AD card) safely — needed at time of filing suit","Wait mandatory 2 months from date of receipt before filing suit","Attach all supporting documents referenced in the notice","Verify noticee's correct designation and office address"]}

